WEBVTT

00:02:28.142 --> 00:02:30.587
I've had the great honor of getting to meet

00:02:30.587 --> 00:02:33.702
some of these, who we would call heroes,

00:02:33.702 --> 00:02:35.604
who have put themselves and put their lives

00:02:35.604 --> 00:02:37.203
at risk to save others,

00:02:37.203 --> 00:02:39.706
and I asked them, "Why would you do it?

00:02:39.706 --> 00:02:41.759
Why did you do it?"

00:02:41.759 --> 00:02:44.660
And they all say the same thing:

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.760
"Because they would have done it for me."

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.667
It's this deep sense of trust and cooperation.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.266
So trust and cooperation are really important here.

00:02:52.266 --> 00:02:55.425
The problem with concepts of trust and cooperation

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:57.730
is that they are feelings, they are not instructions.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.765
I can't simply say to you, "Trust me," and you will.